From 2a0b0f5f7845449653c4251f1a2e72e794e4fded Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jared Wyles <jared.wyles@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:52:39 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 26/32] tests: per-call cost of ordinary vs row-list decode
 attention

test-flash-attn-rows-perf chains attention nodes the way a model's
layers run them and reads the backend's command timing, so one number
per call compares the ordinary kernel with row lists laid out as the
unified pool lays them out: one run, 64-cell chunks, one run per row,
and a padded tail. Small enough for the full Metal profiler.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QA3dWey3RBtBgDz1Tery9Y
